# Wild PDF corpus — REAL user documents, local only, NEVER committed.
# Founder ruling 2026-07-28: "the disk is full of wild PDF. you can use those.
# as long as the PDF file don't go to the public opensource repo".
# The harness is committed; the documents are not.
tests/fixtures/wild/

# OCR engine — vendored locally, NOT committed while the OCR spec is unruled.
# MEASURED runtime payload 5.01 MB (tesseract.min.js 0.06 + worker.min.js 0.12
# + tesseract-core-simd-lstm.wasm.js 3.76 + ind.traineddata 1.07), read off the
# network on a real run, not from the docs. That is +10% on the 4.55 MB the OCR
# spec quotes, and it nearly doubles js/vendor/. Apache-2.0 throughout, so the
# licence is fine; the PAYLOAD is the open question and it is Fauzan's.
# Fetch with scripts/fetch-ocr-engine.sh. Delete these two lines to ship it.
js/vendor/tesseract/
